+
+| ID | Severity | Location | Finding | Rule/FR | Status | Resolution |
+|----|----------|----------|---------|---------|--------|------------|
+| R-01 | Major | cms/src/seed/countries.ts:73-150 | The bands are now written with `documents().update({ status: 'draft' })`. I checked this in `@strapi/core/dist/services/document-service/repository.js:394-442`: `setStatusToDraft` plus a status other than `published` writes the draft only and never calls `publish()`. The code calls `publish()` only when a published version exists and `shouldPublishAfterBackfill` returns true. Otherwise it logs a warning that names the country. A draft-only document is never published. `publish()` copies the whole draft, including its `updatedAt`, into a new published row with `publishedAt = now` (`entries.js:159-181`). So right after a normal publish, draft `updatedAt` ≤ `publishedAt`, and an editor edit made later puts the draft ahead. The heuristic is sound for documents changed only through the admin. Its timestamps are read before the backfill's own DB writes. Idempotence holds: after one run the draft has bands and both rows have currency and locale, so `pricingPatch` is `{}`. In the warning case, `bandsPatch` is taken from the draft, which now has bands, so the warning does not repeat on later boots. The doc comment has been corrected. One remaining path can still publish pending changes: see R-15. | research R5, strapi-conventions | Resolved (bbb742a) | The remaining path is tracked as R-15. |
+| R-03 | Minor | commit 699548d | The intermediate commit does not build on its own. | Constitution | Won't fix (accepted by the human at Gate 3, same as US-01 R-17) | — |
+| R-04 | Minor | frontend/angular.json:38, 52-53; plan-list.page.scss:1 | `node_modules/swiper/swiper.css` is in the build `styles` array, before `src/styles.scss`, so our tokens and the `.plan-list` overrides win. The component `@use` is removed, and the budget is back to 6 kB / 8 kB. I checked the 5.9 kB global file for leaks. Every rule is scoped to `.swiper*` classes, which only the plan list uses. The exceptions are a `:root { --swiper-theme-color }` variable (overridden in `.plan-list`, read by nothing else), a `:host` rule (matches nothing in a document stylesheet) and a `@keyframes swiper-preloader-spin`. Nothing styles other pages. The trade-off: every route now downloads the 5.9 kB, which the human accepted. | Constitution §3.2, T001 | Resolved (b086a30) | I did not run the production build. The 8 kB error limit was confirmed only by reading the config. |
